% Load image and convert to grayscale
img = imread('image.jpg');
grayImg = rgb2gray(img);

% Define Gaussian kernel with standard deviation of 3 pixels
[gaussKernel, gaussSize] = fspecial('gaussian', [5 5], 3);

% Convolve Gaussian filter with grayscale image
filteredImg = imfilter(grayImg, gaussKernel, 'replicate');

% Define Sobel operators for x and y directions
sobelX = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobelY = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];

% Apply Sobel operator to filtered image
edgeImgX = conv2(double(filteredImg), sobelX, 'same');
edgeImgY = conv2(double(filteredImg), sobelY, 'same');

% Combine edges in both directions
edgeImg = sqrt(edgeImgX.^2 + edgeImgY.^2);

% Display edge image
imshow(edgeImg);
```

In this example, we're using a Gaussian kernel with a standard deviation of 3 pixels (you can adjust this value based on the level of smoothing you want). We're also using `imfilter()` instead of `conv2()` to perform the Gaussian filtering, since `imfilter()` is more efficient for large images. Finally, we're applying the Sobel operator to the filtered image instead of the original grayscale image. This should help reduce noise in the input image before detecting edges.

