In order to retrieve the username from the JWT (JSON Web Token) in ASP.NET C# WebAPI, you can follow these steps:

1. Install the `JwtBearer` package by running the following command in your project's console:
   ```
   dotnet add package Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens
   ```

2. In your Startup.cs file, configure the middleware for JWT authentication and authorization. Here's an example:
   ```csharp
   services.AddAuthentication(options =>
   {
       options.DefaultAuthenticateScheme = JwtBearerDefaults.AuthenticationScheme;
       options.DefaultChallengeScheme = JwtBearerDefaults.AuthenticationScheme;
   })
   .AddJwtBearer(options =>
   {
       options.TokenValidationParameters = new TokenValidationParameters
       {
           ValidateIssuer = true,
           ValidIssuer = "https://example.com",
           ValidateAudience = true,
           ValidAudience = "api",
           IssuerSigningKey = new SymmetricSecurityKey(Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes("supersecret_key")),
           ClockSkew = TimeSpan.Zero
       };
   });
   ```

3. Create a custom `AuthorizationFilterAttribute` that will extract the username from the JWT token:
   ```csharp
   public class GetUsernameFromJwt : AuthorizationFilterAttribute
   {
       private readonly string _claimType;

       public GetUsernameFromJwt(string claimType = "http://schemas.microsoft.com/identity/claims/name")
       {
